		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=5107#p5107"><![CDATA[
Moment of inertia is definitely the most "ad-hoc" aspect of our simulation, as the dynamics model for each body is a single stick -- which means that the mass distribution will always be symmetrical (reflected across the stick axis).<br><br>In practice we just use a stick that's as long as the longest body dimension, it seems to feel fairly natural -- if anyone knows of how to calculate this properly, it would be great.. so far we're just using the stick length to model moment of inertia.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=748">raigan2</a> — Mon Aug 20, 2007 3:28 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
